---
description: Safety rules for scanning, moving, and undoing files. Tests never touch the real Downloads folder.
alwaysApply: true
---

# Move safety

- Scan and move only files sitting directly in the chosen folder. Do not walk subfolders.
- Do not move a row the user left unchecked. Do not move anything before an explicit confirm.
- Never overwrite. On a name clash, keep both as `name (1).ext`, then `name (2).ext`.
- Skip partial downloads and junk before they become movable rows: `.crdownload`, `.part`, `.tmp`, `.download`, `desktop.ini`, `thumbs.db`, `~$*`, and dotfiles.
- Every applied move is appended to an undo log stored outside the folder being sorted. Undo restores that run, including collision renames, and removes empty folders that run created.
- Tests and manual checks use a temporary folder. Do not point a test at the real Downloads folder.

```
Bad: shutil.move(src, dest) when dest already exists.
Good: if dest exists, move to "report (1).pdf" and record both paths in the undo log.
```
